{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr6r3yco9dm","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"stride agnostic contact discovery from world model movement lattice","summary":"Run-27: bump/contact discovery no longer assumes UNIT-STEP adjacency. Stride is inferred from the adopted world-model program: _player_delta_map replays program.step over legal_actions and records each action's true-magnitude axis-aligned player delta (cached per program); _movement_stride = min nonzero L-inf magnitude (1 unit, N stride-N); _reachable_player_cells BFSes the model to enumerate the movement lattice. _bump_contexts is redefined: for each object cell and movement delta, walk back one cell at a time (bounded by one stride) to the nearest LATTICE cell whose single full-magnitude move's swept path (via _swept_path) crosses the object; that lattice cell is the approach and the model delta is the bump direction. For a unit mover this reduces to old adjacency. The old unit-step filter in _movement_direction_map (only kept (1,0)/(0,1) deltas) was the root cause: a stride-N mover's deltas were all discarded so dir_map was empty and every bump skipped. New telemetry: movement_stride, reachable_cell_count, contact_probes_probed/found. Stride-2 regression toy: player moves 2/action on even columns, target on odd column (0,3) reachable only by CROSSING (0,2)->(0,4); asserts stride=2 inferred, contact probes fire, level transition detected; old unit-step code fires 0 probes (no unit bump direction has a stride-2 action).","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-04T19:24:24.360Z","vec":[-0.08389539271593094,-0.1086156964302063,-0.029237324371933937,-0.059366483241319656,0.039831362664699554,-0.029923010617494583,-0.01515475008636713,0.004377886652946472,0.04284805431962013,0.02132238820195198,0.048999886959791183,-0.022636521607637405,-0.011544889770448208,0.005021905526518822,-0.020733457058668137,-0.014549282379448414,0.0032737620640546083,0.011644464917480946,-0.0